Hello!

I'm trying to fit point count model to counts of geckos in transects on small islet.

My "sites" are the division of the transects. The geckos are small and move very little so I can treat each division as independent. However, the transects were defined with relation to the habitat, I would like that base-line (the intercept) of the detectability and the Poisson rate to vary with the transect.

I coded a model with Co-variables but it wasn't able to capture any variation of the detectability. I've tried simulations with a simpler model, with just the intercepts and without co-variables, and again doesn't seem to capture any variation.

Any ideas why the model isn't working? Anything I should be reading?

I'm attaching the R script with the simulations if anyone one try. And the model is as follows:

model {
#Point Count Model with random intercepts
#Hyper-Priors
#for the distribution of the intercepts of the poisson rate parameter
a0_p ~ dunif(0, 1)
a0_mu <- 1/(1 + exp(-a0_p))
a0_sd  ~ dexp(1)
a0_tau <- pow(a0_sd, -2)

#for the distribution of the intercepts in detectability
b0_p ~ dunif(0, 1)
b0_mu <- 1/(1 + exp(-b0_p))
b0_sd  ~ dexp(1)
b0_tau <- pow(b0_sd, -2)

#Priors
for (t in 1:NT){
  a0[t] ~ dnorm(a0_mu, a0_tau)
  b0[t] ~ dnorm(b0_mu, b0_tau)
}

#model
for (s in 1:nsite){
  #Poisson process
  log(lambda[s]) <- inprod(a0[], Trs[s,])
  N[s] ~ dpois(lambda[s])

  #Observation model
  p[s] <- logit(inprod(b0[], Trs[s,]))
  for (j in 1:J){
    y[s,j] ~ dbin(p[s], N[s])
  }
}
}

Any help and/or insight would be very much appreciated

Cheers

